.TH CONDUCTOR-PROVISIONER 8 "2026-10-20" "Samba Conductor" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
conductor-provisioner \- delegated Active Directory writes for Samba Conductor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B conductor-provisioner
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B conductor-provisioner
holds a least-privilege account delegated on the managed OUs of a Samba
Active Directory domain and executes typed operations for conductor over a
local socket: one-time invitation and password reset tokens, password set,
lockout clear, account enable, and the Google-first plan operations
(create, update, move, enable and disable of marked accounts). Every
target must be below a configured OU and not privileged; hourly ceilings
and a daily limit per account apply; every change and refusal is recorded
in a hash-chained audit log. Each command accepts
.B \-\-config
.I FILE
(default
.IR /etc/conductor-provisioner/provisioner.toml ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the API for conductor (started by
.BR conductor-provisioner-api.socket ).
.TP
.B status
Configuration summary, tokens by state, audit rows and, with the state
key, whether the audit chain is intact. Run as root.
.TP
.B audit verify | audit export
Check the audit hash chain with the state key, or write the audit log as
JSON lines. Run as root.
.TP
.B delegation preview \-\-ou DN \fR[\fB\-\-account-sid\fR \fISID\fR] [\fB\-\-google-first\fR]
Print the
.B samba-tool dsacl set
commands that delegate the OU to the configured account.
.TP
.B healthcheck
Exit 0 when the configuration loads and the API socket exists.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 error, 2 usage, 3 the audit chain is broken.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/conductor-provisioner/provisioner.toml
Configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/conductor-provisioner/credentials/
.B account-password
and
.BR state-key ,
loaded by systemd.
.TP
.I /var/lib/conductor-provisioner/
State database (token hashes, audit log).
.TP
.I /run/conductor-provisioner/api.sock
The API socket (group conductor).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR conductor (8),
.BR samba-tool (8)
